# Game play UI

When creating or editing `packages/client/src/games/**`:

1. Read [`.agents/design/game-ui.md`](../../.agents/design/game-ui.md).
2. Wrap the view in **`GameShell`** from `components/game-shell` — never a custom full-page background. `GameShell` already applies `app-night-page` (Midnight). Never use legacy `--bg-page` violet gradients.
3. Use **`GamePlayHeader`** for title (top-left) + leave/restart; **`GameOverModal`** on terminal phase (confetti + rankings + restart/leave).
4. **Card-driven prompts** (declare, target, reveal, tuck, guess): use **`GameCardActionModal`** — hero card (~6.5rem) + title/hint + `PlayerIdentity` + body + footer. Never invent a compact Dialog / bare `fixed inset-0` box with a tiny side card. Refs: Love Letter / Salem select-modals, Spicy declare. Portaled dialogs **must** use `room-night-dialog` + `room-night-dialog-overlay` (GameCardActionModal / GameOverModal already do) — otherwise legacy purple `.modal` appears.
5. Put board/hand UI in **`.card`** sections; use theme tokens (`var(--bg-*)`, `var(--text-*)` **after** `app-night-page` remaps them), not hardcoded page gradients.
6. **Tailwind first.** Prefer Tailwind utility classes in the component (`className` + `cn()` from `utils/cn`). Only add or extend a co-located `*.css` when Tailwind cannot express it cleanly (e.g. complex keyframes, board % overlays on printed art, pseudo-elements tied to layout labs). Do not default new UI to a game CSS file.
7. Dev layout labs (`/dev/*-layout`) must root with `app-night-page` — see [board-layout-lab.md](../../.agents/design/board-layout-lab.md).
